    {
      "tag": "v1.0.0",
      "name": "LogcatOn v1.0.0",
      "publishedAt": "2026-06-07T07:53:39Z",
      "htmlUrl": "https://github.com/qwerfunch/logcat-on-releases/releases/tag/v1.0.0",
      "prerelease": false,
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "",
          "category": "other",
          "items": [],
          "paragraphs": [
            "LogcatOn is a desktop Android logcat viewer and debugging tool for macOS, Windows, and Linux. It keeps up with high-volume log streams and ties your logs to what the app is actually doing."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Highlights",
          "category": "other",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Built for volume.</strong> 1M+ lines at 60 fps, even through 5,000-line/sec bursts.",
            "<strong>Filter that follows your app.</strong> Pick a package once; PID/TID rebinds across restarts and crashes.",
            "<strong>Logs meet metrics.</strong> CPU, memory, jank, and battery on a timeline aligned with your logs.",
            "<strong>Signals surface themselves.</strong> 32 patterns flag crashes, ANRs, and native faults — the Issues tray jumps to each.",
            "<strong>Drive the app from the viewer.</strong> Drag-drop install, then launch, force-stop, or uninstall.",
            "<strong>Zero setup.</strong> Bundled adb/aapt2/bundletool; signed auto-updates."
          ],
          "paragraphs": [
            "Also: filtering (level/text/regex/tag/PID/TID/smart-query), bookmarks, find, command palette, dark/light themes, and a UI in English, 한국어, 简体中文, and 日本語 (auto-detects your OS language)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Requirements",
          "category": "other",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Device.</strong> An Android device or emulator with USB debugging enabled — no Android SDK required.",
            "<strong>Java.</strong> JRE 8+ only for <code>.aab</code>/<code>.apks</code> installs; <code>.apk</code>/<code>.xapk</code> and log viewing need none."
          ],
          "paragraphs": []
        },
        {
          "title": "Downloads",
          "category": "other",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Windows</strong> — .msi installer or portable .zip",
            "<strong>macOS</strong> — .dmg (universal arm64+x86_64, signed &amp; notarized) or portable .tar.gz",
            "<strong>Linux</strong> — .AppImage / .deb or portable .tar.gz"
          ],
          "paragraphs": []
        }
      ],
